    git apply <this-file>            # or `git apply --check` first
Then run: python -m pytest tests/upgrade/test_daedalus_client.py

WHAT IT FIXES (audit items 1 and 4):
* item 1 - a long hand-off is no longer reported as failure. _solve now sends a
  server-side `wait` (just under its own budget, capped at Pionir's 600 s max) and,
  on a 202/"running" answer, polls GET /api/task/<id>?wait=60 until the job finishes
  or its deadline passes, returning the real result. Bryo had 0 upgrade_authored
  because its one attempt died at exactly Pionir's 600 s limit and it then read an
  empty diff. Mirrors galatea/hands.py's poll-on-running client logic.
* item 4 - the authoring run marks itself `deferrable: true`, so a stressed Bryo can
  pace it (deferrable had no callers before).

This is the smallest change confined to daedalus_client.py + its test; no refactor.
It also relies on the Pionir-side fix that a running response now carries an explicit
`running: true` field (server.py), which _running() reads.

